urine examination is negative for infections. Ultrasound scan of the bladder, ureter and kidneys is
inconclusive, except a residual volume of 125cc. Which one of the following is the most appropriate
treatment option for her?',NULL,'E','This woman has signs and symptoms of both stress incontinence and urge incontinence, namely
mixed incontinence. However, she is annoyed mostly by the urge. For women with urge continence
as the most bothersome symptom, bladder training would be the most appropriate management
option to consider first. The goals are:
Establishing a baseline with a bladder diary
Establishing a voiding interval
Gradually increasing the voiding interval in increments such as 2–5 minutes over a prolonged
time period aiming to void every 3 hours
Other important measures to consider are lifestyle modifications such as decreased fluid intake,
weight reduction and avoiding certain foods and beverages that have diuretics effects (e.g.,
alcoholic beverages, caffeine, etc).
(Option A) Anticholinergics, combined with continued bladder training, are an option when urge
incontinence does not respond to physical or behavioral therapies. A trial of 4 to 6 weeks is used.
For those who respond, risk and benefits are balanced at 6 months to determine whether treatment
should be continued. Patients should be advised about the adverse effects of anticholinergics such
as dry mouth and constipation, and how to manage them.
(Option B) Anterior coloprrhaphy is a repair of the front vaginal wall to treat cystocele and can help
women who suffer from urinary incontinence. Without a cystocele, bladder neck suspension is the
treatment of choice.
(Option C) Retropubic suspension of the bladder is a more invasive procedure used for treatment
of stress urinary incontinence in patients who has failed to respond to more conservative
measures such as pelvic floor exercise.',NULL,'Retain the source-era answer for question-bank study; verify current Australian guidance before clinical use.',NULL,NULL,'2023','v2.9.4',1,'text','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-823591a04f83","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"250c5f0987cfca256ff0","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":1904,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET source_id=excluded.source_id,source_question_no=excluded.source_question_no,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,system=excluded.system,topic=excluded.topic,clinical_task=excluded.clinical_task,stem_en=excluded.stem_en,answer_key=excluded.answer_key,source_explanation_en=excluded.source_explanation_en,memory_rule_en=excluded.memory_rule_en,image_ref=excluded.image_ref,source_year=excluded.source_year,import_version=excluded.import_version,active=1,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk;
