A 52-year-old man presents to your clinic, seeking
advice on screening for colon cancer. Although he
has no gastrointestinal symptoms, he is concerned
because his younger brother has been recently
diagnosed with colon cancer at the age of 50 years.
There is no other family history of colorectal cancer.
